From: Tommi <tommi@webrtc.org>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 14:32:40 +0200
Subject: (cherry-pick-branch-heads/8103) [M157] Avoid reusing released
 decoders after SetDecoders()

Original change's description:
> Avoid reusing released decoders after SetDecoders()
>
> SetDecoders() only deregistered decoders that were removed or changed,
> but it also reset the decoder database's active payload type. The next
> frame then released the active decoder and configured the same instance
> again. Not all decoders support that: Chromium's hardware decoders fail
> Configure() after Release() and permanently fall back to software
> decoding. This happens e.g. when the receiving side creates a new offer,
> since that typically changes the set of receive codecs.
>
> Deregister all of the previous decoders instead, so that the factory
> creates new instances on demand. This matches how decoders were handled
> before the receive stream stopped being recreated on decoder changes
> (https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/494540).
>
